#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0373 expect=violation domain=ADTTE1
#note "Split-named ADaM dataset reached by an explicit Scope.Domains glob. The rule is scoped Include:['ADTTE*']; ADTTE1 carries no DOMAIN column, so it is not a split in the SDTM sense and the base-name re-test cannot help — only the glob reaches it. Under the retired Include:['ADTTE'] literal this dataset was out of scope."
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when CNSR is not present in an ADTTE (time-to-event) dataset.
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADTTE1
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col AVAL    type=Num  label="Analysis Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | TTDTH | 120
---
